@model DeploymentReadinessViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Settings";
}
<div class="data-banner"><strong>ADMINISTRATOR SETTINGS</strong><span>Read-only production-readiness controls and effective backend boundaries.</span></div>
<section class="settings-grid">
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">DEPLOYMENT TOPOLOGY</span><h3>HA readiness guard</h3></div></div><label>Configured mode<div class="fake-input">@Model.Mode <span>@Model.Status</span></div></label><label>Multi-node readiness<div class="fake-input">@(Model.Mode == DeploymentTopology.MultiNode ? "Requested" : "Blocked until shared state exists") <span>@(Model.Ready ? "Safe" : "Blocked")</span></div></label><p>@Model.Message</p><div class="lab-rule state-warning"><span>!</span><div><strong>Node-local state still present</strong><p>@string.Join(" · ", Model.NodeLocalState)</p></div></div></article>
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">COLLECTION</span><h3>Snapshot policy</h3></div></div><label>Default collection interval<div class="fake-input">30 seconds <span>Backend policy</span></div></label><label>Dashboard delivery<div class="fake-input">Centralized snapshot <span>Required</span></div></label><p>Visual heartbeat timing is independent from SQL collection frequency. Multi-node scheduler ownership is intentionally unsupported until distributed coordination exists.</p></article>
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SECURITY</span><h3>Credential boundaries</h3></div></div><label>Development Admin<div class="fake-input">PBKDF2-SHA256 hash <span>120k iterations</span></div></label><label>SQL Login secrets<div class="fake-input">Backend secret boundary <span>No UI echo</span></div></label><p>Runtime SQL credentials and login-throttling state remain process-local; external secret references can be restart-safe, but they do not make the application multi-node safe.</p></article>
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">REAL-TIME DELIVERY</span><h3>SignalR readiness</h3></div></div><label>Current mode<div class="fake-input">Snapshot reads <span>No widget SQL</span></div></label><p>SignalR remains delivery-only when introduced; it must never invoke collectors or change collection frequency.</p></article>
</section>
